I told you.

258
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:44,112
Well, I've got to admit, I'm surprised
you don't even have a single bruise.

259
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:46,437
This is the first time
this has ever happened.

260
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:49,932
No opponent of mine is standing
after an attack like that.

261
00:19:50,220 --> 00:19:51,760
As true as that may be,

262
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:56,296
you've never fought against me before,
so who's eating their words now?

263
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:06,620
Oh, right.

264
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:13,220
This guy's entire body is a blade, so
his blades don't have a front or a back.

265
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:18,920
Sparkling danger!

266
00:20:26,020 --> 00:20:28,120
This is crazy!

267
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:30,660
Goodbye!

268
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:05,400
When it comes to training, I've
done more than anyone else.

269
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:10,717
I've also been pushed to the
brink in plenty of bad situations,

270
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:12,340
but always succeeded.

271
00:21:13,660 --> 00:21:16,860
But what is it that I
lack to beat this guy?

272
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:20,760
Sensei! Sensei!

273
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:23,630
Hmm?

274
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:28,757
Is it true there are swordsmen in this
world who can cut anything, even steel?

275
00:21:28,840 --> 00:21:29,670
Well, is it?

276
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:34,560
Yes, it certainly is.

277
00:21:36,180 --> 00:21:37,360
Now pay attention.

278
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:40,759
I want you to watch this
paper very carefully, Zoro.

279
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:44,310
Ha!

280
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,504
Sensei, you didn't even cut it.

281
00:21:49,040 --> 00:21:52,511
Listen, Zoro, this is an
important lesson for you to learn.

282
00:21:53,300 --> 00:21:57,124
There are swordsmen out there who
are capable of cutting nothing.

283
00:21:58,120 --> 00:22:01,240
However, these same swordsmen
can also cut anything,

284
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:04,540
and that includes steel,
using the same sword.

285
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:07,377
The strongest swordsmen
in the world are able

286
00:22:07,460 --> 00:22:09,337
to protect that which
they want to protect,

287
00:22:09,420 --> 00:22:11,832
but also cut that which they want to cut.

288
00:22:13,120 --> 00:22:15,837
Sword play that always
harms whatever it touches.

289
00:22:15,920 --> 00:22:18,660
Well, Zoro, that's not real swordsmanship.

290
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:20,720
Do you understand?

291
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:36,313
Sensei, I'm going to be a
swordsman who can cut anything.

292
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:40,318
Zoro, were you listening at
all to what I was saying?

293
00:22:50,540 --> 00:22:54,180
Well what are you waiting for
hurry up and attack me again?

294
00:22:54,860 --> 00:22:58,320
You'll never win if all you do is defend!

295
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:02,737
Trust me pal there's
nothing i'd rather do more

296
00:23:02,820 --> 00:23:04,757
right now than that but
my hands are a little Full

297
00:23:04,840 --> 00:23:10,697
at the moment and it

298
00:23:10,780 --> 00:23:12,157
wasn't a threat it was a

299
00:23:12,240 --> 00:23:15,520
promise i'm gonna cut
steel and you're gonna die!

300
00:23:16,620 --> 00:23:20,780
I highly doubt it she
won't be alive to see it?

301
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:30,920
Large or small i'll cut
everything into pieces.

302
00:23:36,460 --> 00:23:38,140
Swordplay that cuts nothing.

303
00:23:38,580 --> 00:23:39,797
What the hell did that mean?

304
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:40,710
Think.

305
00:23:40,793 --> 00:23:43,420
Cut nothing but cut steel.

306
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:46,160
It doesn't make any sense at all.

307
00:23:48,060 --> 00:23:49,460
Thrust and thrust.

308
00:23:49,920 --> 00:23:52,257
That's the secret of powerful swordplay.

309
00:23:52,340 --> 00:23:53,920
Atomic spawn!

310
00:23:56,620 --> 00:23:58,738
You're not the only one who can cut!

311
00:24:51,040 --> 00:24:53,275
You're really starting to piss me off.

312
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:56,677
The feelings mutual.

313
00:24:56,760 --> 00:25:01,172
Perhaps we'd be evenly matched if I
were a pathetic swordsman, but I'm not.

314
00:25:01,460 --> 00:25:04,280
My weapons are far
nastier than mere swords.

315
00:25:04,660 --> 00:25:06,300
Take this one for example.

316
00:25:12,300 --> 00:25:13,400
Spiral Hollow.

317
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:19,580
Geez, what are you?

318
00:25:19,800 --> 00:25:20,960
An excavator?

319
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:23,220
An assassin, actually.

320
00:25:27,040 --> 00:25:27,870
Sparks!

321
00:25:27,953 --> 00:25:30,293
Just how fast are those blades spinning?

322
00:25:32,800 --> 00:25:33,640
Oh, no!

323
00:25:35,940 --> 00:25:38,800
However, I don't mind
being called an excavator.

324
00:25:39,140 --> 00:25:41,964
Because I'm going to be
digging out your organs.

325
00:25:59,080 --> 00:26:01,962
There's only one thing
left for you after defeat.

326
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:04,470
Death.

327
00:26:25,960 --> 00:26:28,100
I'm surprised you're still alive.

328
00:26:33,440 --> 00:26:36,320
I will not show my back to him.

329
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:39,977
What are you going to fight with?

330
00:26:40,060 --> 00:26:40,890
Your hands?

331
00:26:45,080 --> 00:26:45,910
Stop!

332
00:26:47,080 --> 00:26:47,910
Break!

333
00:27:04,580 --> 00:27:06,420
Die in peace.

334
00:27:09,580 --> 00:27:14,200
I've had bad luck with stones today.

335
00:27:32,660 --> 00:27:36,240
I wonder if the rest of them are okay.

336
00:27:51,660 --> 00:27:52,800
That's impossible.

337
00:27:53,980 --> 00:27:55,940
I cut him so many times.

338
00:27:56,580 --> 00:27:58,815
Did he dodge all those falling stones?

339
00:28:05,220 --> 00:28:06,580
Is that what I did?

340
00:28:07,320 --> 00:28:08,220
Dodge them?

341
00:28:09,380 --> 00:28:10,210
No.

342
00:28:10,840 --> 00:28:15,500
I was just able to sense the
place where no stones would fall.

343
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:21,100
My swords.

344
00:28:22,060 --> 00:28:24,017
One of them is underneath that stone.

345
00:28:24,100 --> 00:28:25,940
I feel it.

346
00:28:29,520 --> 00:28:30,800
What is he doing?

347
00:28:39,960 --> 00:28:42,280
I've experienced this feeling before.

348
00:28:47,160 --> 00:28:51,177
Everything goes quiet around me so

349
00:28:51,260 --> 00:28:54,800
quiet i can hear my heartbeat so clearly.

350
00:28:57,020 --> 00:29:01,260
Is this is this what it feels
like when you're close to death?

351
00:29:03,320 --> 00:29:06,637
It was almost like like
those falling stones

352
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:10,000
gave me a hint as if
they were living things.

353
00:29:11,660 --> 00:29:13,440
No, it wasn't a hint.

354
00:29:13,840 --> 00:29:15,800
It was much clearer than that.

355
00:29:16,280 --> 00:29:18,620
It was like... rhythm.

356
00:29:20,080 --> 00:29:21,497
Could it be...

357
00:29:21,580 --> 00:29:23,227
trees have their own rhythm?

358
00:29:25,600 --> 00:29:26,717
So does soil.

359
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:28,220
Is that what it is?

360
00:29:29,920 --> 00:29:32,567
This is an important
lesson for you to learn.

361
00:29:32,980 --> 00:29:37,156
Zoro, there are swordsmen out there
who are capable of cutting nothing.

362
00:29:38,940 --> 00:29:42,877
Does cutting nothing mean
hearing the rhythm of the things

363
00:29:42,960 --> 00:29:46,877
around you if so is that how

364
00:29:46,960 --> 00:29:51,717
one can Cut steel what the

365
00:29:51,800 --> 00:29:56,997
hell did you do after a vicious
attack like that and all

366
00:29:57,080 --> 00:30:00,609
the blood you've lost There's
no way you can still be alive.

367
00:30:00,960 --> 00:30:02,200
I hear it.

368
00:30:02,600 --> 00:30:03,440
His steel.

369
00:30:04,060 --> 00:30:05,500
It has a rhythm.

370
00:30:06,900 --> 00:30:09,600
Just like everything else around me.

371
00:30:25,020 --> 00:30:25,850
Alright.

372
00:30:26,720 --> 00:30:27,550
Fine.

373
00:30:27,633 --> 00:30:30,559
When I'm done, you're going
to wish you stayed down.

374
00:30:32,340 --> 00:30:34,260
Only one question remains.

375
00:30:35,160 --> 00:30:38,140
Do I really have the ability to cut steel?

376
00:30:38,560 --> 00:30:42,020
Well, there's only one way to find out.

377
00:30:42,340 --> 00:30:44,046
You failed with three swords.

378
00:30:44,320 --> 00:30:46,555
Can you defend yourself with only one?

379
00:30:47,180 --> 00:30:50,120
I won't defend.

380
00:30:51,540 --> 00:30:54,420
So you're prepared to die!

381
00:30:59,040 --> 00:31:04,460
One-sword style, Lion
Strike, Atomic Splendor!

382
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:25,830
Thanks to you.

383
00:31:27,700 --> 00:31:29,980
I've finally reached the next level.

384
00:31:35,740 --> 00:31:42,500
I don't know how, but he learned how
to do it, just like he said he would.

385
00:31:46,420 --> 00:31:52,280
Now that you've cut steel,
what's next for you, Diamonds?

386
00:31:54,280 --> 00:31:55,110
No.

387
00:31:55,193 --> 00:31:56,160
That'd be a waste.

388
00:31:57,760 --> 00:31:59,580
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

389
00:31:59,920 --> 00:32:00,900
Good luck.
